  "task": {
    "objective": "Deliver each boat cargo to its indexed dock using either lock lane and the two shared transferable water units.",
    "natural_termination": "All three boats delivered; otherwise truncate at tick 128, with natural completion taking priority on that tick.",
    "interaction": "A chamber may be opened at the low bank only at level zero and at the high bank only at level two. Filling or transferring water changes what the other chamber can do. Boats physically occupy cells, may form convoys and may need to yield an entrance to allow opposing traffic.",
    "observation_access": "All map, boat, gate, chamber, reservoir and dock state is public. The flat row adds the acting boat identity. No private targets or unobserved resource fields are used.",
    "transition_order": "Movement uses old gate states and rotating occupancy priority. Each chamber then selects one nearby boat command by the same rotating boat priority. Chambers settle their commands in alternating lane order, followed by delivery and termination."
  },
  "invariant_notes": [
    "All active boats occupy distinct navigable cells. Finished boats are inactive and accept only wait.",
    "At every reachable state, sum(level)+stock[0]=2; stock and each chamber level remain in [0,2].",
    "A lane cannot have both gates open; an open low gate implies level zero and an open high gate implies level two.",
    "The low and high basins are fixed reference elevations; the conserved two units model chamber service water, not an unbounded fluid solver.",
    "For each boat cargo+delivered=1, and each indexed dock can be served once.",
    "Selected unsuccessful pump/transfer attempts still incur the declared operator cost; commands are not promises of success.",
    "Raw terminal state is absorbing; actual terminal cause and time are retained."
  ]
